WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.180
An assembly brings together delegations from
many places.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.210
Hundreds of people can take part in the
discussion.

3
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.890
Millions may want to follow it.

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:15.820
How can this meeting organize participation and
distribute its voices without

5
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.950
concentrating all media in one application
server?

6
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:26.800
In PRP, groupcast gives the group its own
reference and participation governed by
authorized identities.

7
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.870
The assembly application decides who may take
the floor.

8
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:36.300
Group membership does not automatically grant
every right to speak or transmit.

9
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.380
Amara presents her proposal. Kenji responds.

10
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.870
Each stream has its own reference and authorized
source.

11
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:48.860
The application associates these streams with
the meeting.

12
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:55.340
The group organizes participants without turning
all their voices into a single source.

13
00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.740
Aggregators distribute each stream along paths
to its recipients.

14
00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.620
Shared stretches can feed further branches.

15
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:09.840
The source does not need to send a separate copy
to every viewer.

16
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.190
Distribution grows through cooperation across
the network.

17
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.530
The assembly chooses which streams to make
public.

18
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.790
Millions can follow without joining the
deliberating group.

19
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:26.100
Carrying these voices does not grant the right
to admit delegates, claim authorship,

20
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.140
or control who may speak.

21
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.830
One stream ends.

22
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.900
Another begins.

23
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.650
Sessions can change while the group continues.

24
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:41.000
This organization depends on valid state,
available paths, and capacity.

25
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.540
Many voices take part.

26
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.030
A larger audience follows.

27
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.510
The group organizes participation.

28
00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.860
The network distributes the streams. Groupcast.
PRP.

